Analyzing the Bridge Problem
I've got the classic bridge crossing puzzle in mind. The core of the issue is figuring out the most efficient way to get four people with varying speeds across the bridge using a single torch, and ensuring no one gets left behind. I'm focusing on minimizing the total time, given the constraint of only two people crossing at once, and the different crossing speeds for each person. The challenge is in optimally pairing people for the return trips.
Optimizing the Crossing Strategy
