The fastest time to get all four people across the bridge is 17 minutes.
Here is the step-by-step breakdown of how to achieve this:
A and B cross the bridge together.
Time taken: 2 minutes (the speed of the slower person).
Total time elapsed: 2 minutes.
A returns with the torch.
Time taken: 1 minute.
Total time elapsed: 3 minutes.
C and D cross the bridge together.
Time taken: 10 minutes (the speed of the slower person).
Total time elapsed: 13 minutes.
B returns with the torch.
Time taken: 2 minutes.
Total time elapsed: 15 minutes.
A and B cross the bridge together.
Time taken: 2 minutes.
Total time elapsed: 17 minutes.
Why this works:
In most logic puzzles like this, the instinct is to have the fastest person (A) shuttle everyone across. However, that forces the two slowest people (C and D) to cross separately, adding 5 and 10 minutes to the total respectively. By having C and D cross together, you "collapse" their times so that the 5-minute person doesn't add any extra time to the trip.
